# Caddy site block for x5.vi0lins.de, next to vanspace.vi0lins.de on the same server.
#
# Unlike vanspace3d (static files only), X5 Commander has a scoreboard API, so Caddy doesn't serve files itself: it
# terminates HTTPS (Let's Encrypt, automatic) and proxies everything to the Node server (server/index.ts), which
# serves the game, the API, gzip, caching and the security headers. The Node server runs as a systemd *user* service
# of the deploy user (deploy/x5-commander.service), so deploys restart it without sudo.
#
# One-time setup on the server (needs sudo, run interactively):
#
#   # Node 22.18+ (24 recommended) as /usr/bin/node, if it isn't there yet (node --version):
#   curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_24.x | sudo -E bash - && sudo apt-get install -y nodejs
#
#   sudo mkdir -p /var/www/x5-commander/releases /var/www/x5-commander/shared
#   sudo chown -R mycaravam:mycaravam /var/www/x5-commander
#   sudo loginctl enable-linger mycaravam      # user services keep running without a login session
#   sudo tee -a /etc/caddy/Caddyfile <<'EOF'
#
#   x5.vi0lins.de {
#           reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8095
#   }
#   EOF
#   sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# DNS: an A/AAAA record (or CNAME to vi0lins.de) for x5.vi0lins.de.
#
# After that, deploys are just (or push to main: .github/workflows/deploy.yml):
#
#   X5_DEPLOY_HOST=mycaravam@vi0lins.de ./deploy/deploy.sh
#
# and rollbacks:
#
#   X5_DEPLOY_HOST=mycaravam@vi0lins.de ./deploy/rollback.sh

x5.vi0lins.de {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8095
}
